What is Pharmacogenomics (PGx)?
Pharmacogenomics (PGx) is a revolutionary field within precision medicine that analyzes how an individual's genetic makeup influences their response to drugs. By merging pharmacology (the science of drugs) with genomics (the study of genes and their functions), PGx enables healthcare providers to develop highly personalized treatment plans. This approach minimizes the traditional trial-and-error method of prescribing, optimizes drug dosages for maximum efficacy, and significantly reduces the risk of adverse drug reactions, thereby improving patient outcomes and safety.
